1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,780
The nearest star to the Sun

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:03,340
is out there tonight.

3
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:05,240
You can't see it.

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,960
It's called Proxima Centauri,

5
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:10,360
a small red dwarf.

6
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:13,780
It gives out less than 1%

7
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:14,880
of the Sun's light.

8
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:17,520
Its light still takes more than

9
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:19,420
four years to reach you.

10
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:21,680
The full film:

11
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:24,440
How Far Is the Nearest Star?
